{"title":"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_-_Common_Sense\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 - Common Sense</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_-_Deriving_a_Formula\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 - Deriving a Formula</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_-_Border_vs._Internal_toothpicks\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 - Border vs. Internal toothpicks</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Toothpicks are used to make a grid that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> toothpicks long and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4b8590f8aa9f9894b3891dd5dede0e354fa04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> toothpicks wide. How many toothpicks are used altogether?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/1/c610668e8c5623b4247005f01744cde6726b65a9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] picture corner; draw(corner,(5,0)--(35,0)); draw(corner,(0,-5)--(0,-35)); for (int i=0; i&lt;3; ++i){for (int j=0; j&gt;-2; --j){if ((i-j)&lt;3){add(corner,(50i,50j));}}} draw((5,-100)--(45,-100)); draw((155,0)--(185,0),dotted+linewidth(2)); draw((105,-50)--(135,-50),dotted+linewidth(2)); draw((100,-55)--(100,-85),dotted+linewidth(2)); draw((55,-100)--(85,-100),dotted+linewidth(2)); draw((50,-105)--(50,-135),dotted+linewidth(2)); draw((0,-105)--(0,-135),dotted+linewidth(2));[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"185\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/f/7ff40ae7d52d007b00b0a0f497473670461c5bec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1920 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 1952 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 1980 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 2013 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 3932$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"484\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/nNDdkv_zfOo\">https://youtu.be/nNDdkv_zfOo</a> ~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/6/866b44935f69a5b800547127fe13210bb1e36fbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$61$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> vertical columns with a length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4b8590f8aa9f9894b3891dd5dede0e354fa04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> toothpicks, and there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6f3bccae16d5e31266370fced24edc41538d5da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$33$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> horizontal rows with a length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> toothpicks, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4b8590f8aa9f9894b3891dd5dede0e354fa04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> are the number of intervals. You can verify this by trying a smaller case, i.e. a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/3/9f3f04882ae10c114ebe301c72ee68990d97c48e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\times 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> grid of toothpicks, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/7/d278803d72fcc493afb1559174a483aa7f41d143.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\times 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/7/ed788f5a1c4203b73faf5ab6bdfb6bfaad745666.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2  \\times 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/a/70a25e6b38549c52f0647cf16c28f5dcb75b8bdc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$61\\cdot 32 + 33 \\cdot 60 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 3932}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"228\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Note by Theraccoon: The person who posted this answer did not include their name. Minor edit by ~NXC\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_-_Common_Sense\">Solution 2 - Common Sense</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 - Common Sense\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>With a quick mental calculation, 60 * 30 yields 1800, which is roughly where 4 of our 5 answer choices lie in. However, we can tell that each square would require at most 2 toothpicks that uniquely belong to itself, so the answer would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/a/86a61bc895108450bdc670782cc15dbf07f68ed6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60\\cdot 30 \\cdot 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> which would be roughly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/2/442fe81ca39f0b57ee5c51c820bb773b2c41bd8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 3932}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"82\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>-pearlseal34, Minor Edit by MagentaButterfly29\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_-_Deriving_a_Formula\">Solution 3 - Deriving a Formula</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 - Deriving a Formula\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If you wanted to find the number of toothpicks in a x by y rectangle you will notice a pattern. We can separate the toothpicks into 2 groups, vertical and horizontal toothpicks and add them together. There is x(y+1) vertical toothpick that are vertical and y(x+1) horizontal toothpicks.If my explantation doesn't make sense try drawing it out. You can add these two for the total amount of toothpicks. Now we can plug in 60 into x and 32 into y and solve. 60(32+1)+32(60+1)= 60(32)+60+32(60)+32=3932 which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/2/442fe81ca39f0b57ee5c51c820bb773b2c41bd8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 3932}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"82\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>-ZenJacob\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_-_Border_vs._Internal_toothpicks\">Solution 4 - Border vs. Internal toothpicks</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 - Border vs. Internal toothpicks\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The total area of the 60 X 32 grid is 1920 square units. If each square was separated, we would need 1920 * 4 = 7680 toothpicks. However, once all the squares are joined to form a grid, each internal toothpick forms the edge of two adjacent squares. The perimeter/border of the grid contains 60 + 60 + 32 + 32 = 184 sticks. So, 7680 - 184 = 7496 toothpicks are internal toothpicks. Since each internal toothpick forms the edge of two adjacent squares, we need only 7496 / 2 = 3748 of them. So, the total toothpicks needed are 3748 (internal) + 184 (border) which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/2/442fe81ca39f0b57ee5c51c820bb773b2c41bd8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 3932}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"82\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>-AbbasK\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8\" title=\"2013 AMC 8\">2013 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2013\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2013 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_8_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 8 Problems and Solutions\"> All AJHSME/AMC 8 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017201629\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.033 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.052 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 165/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2272/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 132/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/10